{
  "id": "26928_inyousuru",
  "headword": "{引用|いんよう}する",
  "reading": "いんようする",
  "romaji": "inyousuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to quote; to cite",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to quote; to cite",
      "explanation": "To reproduce someone else's words, a passage from a text, or data from a source, typically to support an argument or illustrate a point."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26928_inyousuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{有名|ゆうめい}な{詩|し}を{引用|いんよう}した。",
      "english": "I quoted a famous poem.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26928_inyousuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "レポートに{専門家|せんもんか}の{意見|いけん}を{引用|いんよう}した。",
      "english": "I cited an expert's opinion in my report.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26928_inyousuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{他人|たにん}の{文章|ぶんしょう}を{引用|いんよう}する{場合|ばあい}は、{必|かなら}ず{出典|しゅってん}を{明記|めいき}しなければならない。",
      "english": "When citing someone else's writing, you must always clearly state the source.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Used in academic, journalistic, and legal contexts. The noun form {引用|いんよう} is very common and can modify other nouns. Japanese copyright law ({著作権法|ちょさくけんほう}) has specific rules about what constitutes fair {引用|いんよう}.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {引用|いんよう}{文|ぶん}: quotation; cited passage\n- {引用|いんよう}{元|もと}: source of quotation\n- {引用|いんよう}{符|ふ}: quotation marks\n- {出典|しゅってん}を{引用|いんよう}する: to cite a source\n- {無断|むだん}{引用|いんよう}: unauthorized quotation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {参照|さんしょう}する: to refer to; to consult — directing the reader to a source, without reproducing the text\n- {転載|てんさい}する: to reprint; to reproduce — copying and republishing content, often requiring permission\n- {抜粋|ばっすい}する: to excerpt — selecting and extracting a portion of a text",
